# PowerEdge R410 profile.
#
# Chassis notes:
# - 1U with 6× 40mm fans (FAN MOD 1A/B, 2A/B, 3A/B)
# - DANGER: BMC obeys low PWM literally — 5% = 0 RPM (fan stall, zero
#   airflow). No safety clamp like R730xd. MIN_FAN must stay >=15 to
#   avoid stalling. Probed values: 10%=840 RPM (suspicious), 15%=2520
#   RPM (safe minimum), 20%=3600 RPM (current default).
# - No GPU
# - CPUs are Xeon 5500/5600 series, TJunction ~95-100°C
# - IMPORTANT: BMC reports IPMI entity 3.x as "Disabled" — relies on
#   coretemp source via /sys/class/hwmon (controller handles fallback)

: "${MIN_FAN:=20}"             # 20% = 3600 RPM. Probed lower (15% = 2520
                               # RPM) but BMC flagged "lcr" (lower-critical
                               # threshold breach) and IPMI started returning
                               # comms errors. 20% is the operational floor
                               # on R410 — BMC is OK with it.

# Fan-addressing dialect. 11th-gen iDRAC6 (R410/R510/R610/R710) REJECTS
# the 0xff "all fans" broadcast selector with completion code 0xCC
# ("Invalid data field") — that selector is a 12G+ convention. Each fan
# must be addressed by index instead (0x00, 0x01, …). "auto" makes the
# controller try 0xff first and, when the BMC rejects it, discover the
# accepted per-fan indices at startup (this chassis presents 0x00–0x07;
# 5A/5B are unpopulated). Set explicitly (e.g. "0-7") to skip the probe.
: "${FAN_INDICES:=auto}"

# IPMI temperature sensors on R410's iDRAC6. The BMC only exposes a
# single ambient-air sensor ("Ambient Temp", record id 10). Per-CPU
# sensors are listed by the SDR but reported as "Disabled" — coretemp
# via node_hwmon_temp_celsius is the working source. No exhaust sensor
# at all on this chassis; that tile stays empty.
: "${SENSOR_INLET_NAME:=Ambient Temp}"
: "${SENSOR_INLET_ID:=10}"
